1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,280
This is Loop.

2
00:00:01,280 --> 00:00:03,560
Mutual transfers, reimagined.

3
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:07,380
Priya teaches in Pune, and her husband works in Nagpur.

4
00:00:07,380 --> 00:00:11,490
Nobody in Nagpur wants Pune, so a pairs-only portal leaves her stuck.

5
00:00:11,490 --> 00:00:14,600
But a three-way loop exists, and Loop finds it.

6
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:16,080
This is the live market.

7
00:00:16,080 --> 00:00:18,470
Every arc is someone who wants to move.

8
00:00:18,470 --> 00:00:23,270
As the engine finds loops, they light up, and turn green when everyone agrees.

9
00:00:23,270 --> 00:00:28,360
On the same requests, Loop moves several times more people than pair matching.

10
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,770
In Loop Lab, the server builds a whole cadre and runs the real engine twice.

11
00:00:34,770 --> 00:00:37,340
Limited to pairs, only a few people move.

12
00:00:37,340 --> 00:00:42,840
Allow three- and four-way loops, and the same people suddenly have somewhere to go.

13
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:50,400
Let's try it.

14
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:54,510
Sign in with a demo account, and post a request in one tap:

15
00:00:54,510 --> 00:00:57,800
a primary teacher in Pune who wants Nagpur.

16
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:03,950
One tap posts the request.

17
00:01:03,950 --> 00:01:10,530
The server schedules a solve right away, and searches every two-, three- and four-way loop it could join.

18
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:14,850
Seconds later, a three-way loop.

19
00:01:14,850 --> 00:01:19,320
Every seat is locked in one transaction, so no one is ever in two loops.

20
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:20,670
Answers stream in live.

21
00:01:20,670 --> 00:01:24,020
Partners stay anonymous until everyone says yes.

22
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:26,800
The last yes closes the loop.

23
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:32,640
Names and contacts are revealed, with a verification code, and the loop drawn on the map.

24
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:42,030
Loop even prepares the joint transfer application, and a public page where the transfer office can verify that everyone agreed.

25
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:45,100
Pairs are rare.

26
00:01:45,100 --> 00:01:46,370
Loops are everywhere.

27
00:01:46,370 --> 00:01:48,360
Built with Serverpod and Flutter.

28
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:49,390
Try it live.
